---
description: frontend Rust WASM engines (Cargo workspace + JS bridge beside React)
alwaysApply: false
---
Use these rules when a frontend package includes Rust engines compiled to WASM (and optional native CLI pre-generation). Pair with: code-craft, rust-core, `stack-frontend-wasm`, and frontend-core. Attach frontend-http-api + `stack-frontend-http` only if the app also calls HTTP APIs.

### Where these paths live

- All trees below are relative to the **frontend package root**:
  - Frontend-only repo: the package root is the **repo root**.
  - Monorepo: the package root is **`frontend/`**.
- Prefer `apps/web` for the React shell (see frontend-core) — not a top-level `app/` folder.

### Layout

```text
./                                   # frontend package root (FE-only repo root, or frontend/ in monorepo)
├── crates/                          # Cargo workspace — all Rust engine / bridge / CLI code
│   ├── Cargo.toml                   # [workspace] members = [...]
│   ├── rust-toolchain.toml          # Optional: pin channel/targets (incl. wasm32)
│   ├── <engine_crate>/              # e.g. physics_engine — pure Rust, no wasm-bindgen (confirm JS glue crate in stack-frontend-wasm)
│   │   ├── Cargo.toml
│   │   └── src/
│   │       ├── lib.rs
│   │       ├── isostasy.rs          # Example domain modules (name to match domain)
│   │       ├── torque.rs
│   │       └── error.rs             # domain errors (example: thiserror — confirm in stack-frontend-wasm)
│   ├── wasm_bridge/                 # Only crate with JS glue / cdylib (example: wasm-bindgen — confirm in stack-frontend-wasm)
│   │   ├── Cargo.toml               # crate-type = ["cdylib", "rlib"]; depends on engine crates
│   │   └── src/
│   │       ├── lib.rs               # JS exports only (example: #[wasm_bindgen] — confirm in stack-frontend-wasm)
│   │       ├── api.rs               # Thin wrappers over engine types/fns
│   │       └── types.rs             # Optional: JS-facing DTOs (example: serde-wasm-bindgen — confirm in stack-frontend-wasm)
│   └── <cli_crate>/                 # Optional: e.g. worldgen_cli — native offline pre-gen
│       ├── Cargo.toml               # depends on engine crates, not wasm_bridge
│       └── src/
│           └── main.rs              # Reads inputs → runs engine → writes assets
├── src/                             # React features / shared / pages (see frontend-core)
│   └── shared/
│       └── gen/
│           └── wasm/                # generated WASM/JS/TS (do not hand-edit; example builder: wasm-pack — confirm in stack-frontend-wasm)
│               ├── <pkg>.js
│               ├── <pkg>_bg.wasm
│               └── <pkg>.d.ts       # When TS bindings generated
├── apps/
│   └── web/                         # Vite/React (+ Three.js etc.)
│       ├── package.json             # Or rely on root workspace package.json
│       ├── vite.config.ts
│       └── src/                     # App shell only; most UI in ../../src
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
└── ...
```

  - Product names (`physics_engine`, `worldgen_cli`, domain files like `isostasy.rs`) are examples only. Prefer reusable names: `<engine_crate>`, `wasm_bridge`, `<cli_crate>`, domain modules named for the science/model.

### Crate roles (do not conflate)

- **Pure engine crates** (`<engine_crate>/`): core math/simulation. No JS glue crates (example: no wasm-bindgen here — confirm the glue crate in `stack-frontend-wasm`), and no `web-sys` unless truly required. Must be reusable from both the WASM bridge and native CLI.
- **`wasm_bridge/`**: thin FFI only — JS-exported wrappers, input/output conversion. No large domain logic. Depends on engine crates.
- **`<cli_crate>/` (optional)**: native binary for offline pre-generation (science models that write assets). Depends on engine crates, **not** on `wasm_bridge`.

### Boundary and performance

- Prefer a thin JS/TS ↔ Rust surface: numbers, typed arrays / buffers, or small DTOs (example: serde-wasm-bindgen — confirm in `stack-frontend-wasm`). Avoid chatty fine-grained calls in hot loops.
- Keep heavy simulation / generation loops in Rust. React/Three.js owns UI, scene graph, and presentation.
- For realtime in-app simulation: load artifacts from `src/shared/gen/wasm/` via the app bundler; call into `wasm_bridge` APIs from feature hooks/services.
- For offline pre-gen: run `<cli_crate>` (or `cargo run -p <cli_crate>`) to write assets the app loads — do not force pre-generation through WASM.

### Build and generated output

- Build `wasm_bridge` into `src/shared/gen/wasm/` with the toolchain in `stack-frontend-wasm` (example: wasm-pack — confirm there).
- Never hand-edit files under `src/shared/gen/wasm/`; regenerate after Rust API changes.
- Generated artifacts policy: either commit wasm/JS/TS bindings **or** generate in CI — pick one per repo and stay consistent (same idea as protobuf gen).
- Pin the WASM target via `rust-toolchain.toml` or documented toolchain setup when helpful (`wasm32-unknown-unknown`).

### Rust craft inside crates

- Follow rust-core and `stack-frontend-wasm` (domain errors in engines, avoid unwrap in library code, rustfmt/clippy).
- Engine crates may be sync; do not pull the backend async runtime into WASM engines unless required.
- Document `pub` / JS-exported surfaces with rustdoc when they form the JS contract.

### Frontend integration

- Most UI/domain React code still lives under `src/features`, `src/shared`, `src/pages` (frontend-core).
- Prefer a small shared helper or feature service that loads/initializes the WASM module once and exposes typed functions to widgets.
- `apps/web` stays thin: bundler config, WASM plugin wiring if needed, bootstrap.

### Attach presets

- Frontend-only + WASM: `code-craft`, `frontend-core`, `stack-frontend-react`, `rust-core`, `frontend-rust-wasm`, `stack-frontend-wasm`
- Also calling HTTP: add `http-api-contract`, `frontend-http-api`, `stack-frontend-http`
